    "narrative": "With a limited slate today, **Liam Hicks** stands out as the primary offensive engine for the Austin Waves, posting a score of 55.93. While he remains in \"Lineup Pending\" status, the expectation is that he will anchor the middle of the order at #4. His matchup against Shawn Armstrong (xERA 4.35) provides a favorable floor, and when combined with his strong recency bias and a positive platoon adjustment against the right-handed arm, **Liam Hicks** becomes our clear priority play. **Brayan Rocchio** rounds out the active roster with a marginal 49.70 score; while his matchup against Nick Martinez is technically advantageous, his placement at the bottom of the order and a slight negative platoon variance tether him to the lower end of our starting efficiency range.\n\nThe bench remains heavily populated with high-ceiling talent currently sidelined by scheduling or injury. **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Gunnar Henderson** are all inactive today due to team off-days, effectively nullifying any potential contribution to our 5x5 categories. Furthermore, we continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.**, who remains on the IL; his absence remains a significant hurdle for our stolen base production, given our organizational mandate to emphasize elite sprint speed. The decision to prioritize **Liam Hicks** over potential depth options like **Drake Baldwin** or **Nasim Nunez** was dictated by the superior projected order placement and the stability of the matchup against a middling arm like Armstrong. We will continue to manage the remaining depth\u2014including **Andy Pages**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Jordan Westburg**\u2014strictly against favorable xERA matchups to maximize efficiency for the remainder of the week.",
